Evan,

Can you provide the levels of your two variables and the levels of the combined variable?

And what model formula did you when when you separated the effects in the ANOVA?  (I am wondering if you included an interaction term)

I am guessing that when you created the combination, you effectively created a variable with all combinations of levels.  This would amount to a model with main effects + interaction, whereas a model with just the two variables would represent just the main effects.  These would be two different models and the appropriate choice will depend on your assumptions and, as Iara noted, also your question.

Julie

