Hey there!

Specifically in my case we were testing influence of fish scent and toad tadpole presence on behavior of frog tadpoles. For each variable there were only two levels: present or not. When exposed to just fish scent, the frogs had an increased tendency for anti-predatory behaviors.We are now primarily interested in testing to see if toad presence further modifies this change in behavior, with our hypothesis being that the toad presence will lower the tendency.

Our initial ANOVA call was:

aov(behavior ~ Fish+ Fish:Toads)

So this includes just the fish presence effect and the interaction effect.

Afterwards we combined the variables:

treatment = as.factor(paste(Fish,Toads))
aov(behavior ~ treatment)

This differing result was due to how df was determined in the calculations for ANOVA, I feel like it is acceptable given my central interest , but I want to make sure before continuing.

Hopefully this helps clarify the situation.

(In the process of writing this both Julie and Rosemary responded, and Rosemary may have a clearer description of the situation)

Thanks for the help,
Evan

