You're right, I was missing something.  I'm just figuring this out myself, but I think what you want is `vcov(model)`, which contains the variance-covariance matrix of all the regression coefficients.  With this you should be able to get the variance of the trend coefficient, and the square root of that should be your standard error.  That is, if the trend term is linear.  I'm not sure how it works with a polynomial trend.

